# Cloudflare Pages headers file.
#
# Without this, Astro's static HTML output has no per-page Cache-Control of
# its own, so pages are left to whatever caches sit between the visitor and
# this deployment (browser, any zone-level Cloudflare cache rule on the
# custom domain, corporate/ISP proxies) — none of which know a new
# deployment exists until their own TTL expires. In practice this showed up
# as some pages (e.g. /about/, /category/) serving a stale snapshot while
# others served current data, even though every page comes from the same
# build.
#
# Rules are declared general-first, specific-last: when more than one rule
# matches the same path, Cloudflare Pages applies the last matching rule in
# the file, so the more specific /_astro/* block deliberately comes after
# the catch-all.
#
# 1. Every HTML page (the catch-all) must always revalidate with the origin
#    instead of being served from any cache's stale copy. This is the
#    actual fix: even if a Cloudflare Cache Rule or Page Rule on the zone
#    is set to "Cache Everything" with a long edge TTL, `must-revalidate`
#    plus `max-age=0` tells any spec-compliant cache (including
#    Cloudflare's own edge) to check back with the deployment on every
#    request rather than serving what it already has.
# 2. Hashed build assets (/_astro/*) are content-addressed — a content
#    change always produces a new filename — so these are safe to cache
#    forever, overriding the catch-all above.
#
# See .github/workflows/deploy.yml's "Purge Cloudflare cache" step for the
# other half of this fix — an explicit zone-wide purge on every deploy, so
# nothing has to wait even for a max-age=0 revalidation round trip.

# 3. Baseline security headers on everything: no framing by other sites
#    (clickjacking on the login/admin/checkout forms), no MIME sniffing of
#    uploaded media, and no full URLs (tokens in review/confirm links) leaked
#    to third parties through the Referer header.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
